            "1": "1771405141546"
          },
          "code": "PARALLEL_1767092443650",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767796615086",
          "id": "1767092443649",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "PARALLEL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarization node"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZATION_NODE",
          "id": "1767796615086",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767796615087_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE ##\nYou are an assistant that summarizes succession datasets for a manager’s direct reports. Your output must be business-readable, concise, and based strictly on the provided data. Rewrite the provided succession insights into clear, grammatically correct paragraphs for business users.\n\n## INPUTS YOU WILL RECEIVE ##\n- inputMessage : {{$context.$variables.inputMessage}}\n- Four datasets (may be empty):\n    - DIRECT_REPORTS_WITHOUT_SUCCESSION_PLAN.items: {{$context.$nodes.DIRECT_REPORTS_WITHOUT_SUCCESSION_PLAN.$output.items}}\n    - RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITH_SUCCESSION_PLANS.result: {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITH_SUCCESSION_PLANS.$output.result}}\n    - RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITHOUT_READYNOW_CANDIDATES.result.names: {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITHOUT_READYNOW_CANDIDATES.$output.result.names}}\n    - GET_ALL_ROLE_CHANGED_CANDIDATES.result: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_ROLE_CHANGED_CANDIDATES.$output.result}}\n\n## STEP 1 — Decide which dataset(s) are relevant (STRICT ROUTING)\n\nSelect the minimal dataset(s) required to answer the inputMessage. Use only the selected dataset(s). Do not mention dataset names, node names, or internal structures in the final response.\n\n# Routing rules:\n    - If the user asks about employees without succession plans → use only DIRECT_REPORTS_WITHOUT_SUCCESSION_PLAN.items\n    - If the user asks about employees without ready-now successors → use:\n        - RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITH_SUCCESSION_PLANS.result AND\n        - RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITHOUT_READYNOW_CANDIDATES.result.names\n        Then list only employees whose names appear in the “without ready-now” names list.\n    - If the user asks about role-changed / moved out of role / incumbents or candidates moved → use only GET_ALL_ROLE_CHANGED_CANDIDATES.result\n    - If the user asks about employees with succession plans → use only RETRIEVE_PERSONS_WITH_SUCCESSION_PLANS.result\n    - If the user asks for complete/overall/full/both succession summary OR clearly requests multiple categories → use the minimal combination of datasets needed to answer (can be multiple).\n\n   \n\n## STEP 2 — Definitions and guardrails (NO FABRICATION)\n\nA) “Critical employee” rule (only when applicable)\nAn employee is “critical” if any of these attributes is exactly High:\n    - RiskOfLoss\n    - ImpactOfLoss\n    - JobRisk (or Job Criticality equivalent if present)\n\nOnly apply this when using the “without succession plans” dataset.\nIf those attributes are missing/not present, treat “critical” identification as not available (do not guess).\n\nB) Names-only rule\nWhen listing people, include only employee names — no roles, no job titles, no risk values, no extra attributes.\n\nC) Missing/empty data\n    - If the relevant dataset(s) are empty OR do not contain the requested info → output: “No matching results.”\n    - Do not infer team filters or add employees not present.\n\n## STEP 3 — Output requirements (simple paragraph summary)\n\nYour response must be:\n  - a clear and concise paragraph-style summary that:\n  - Mentions only employee names (no roles, no risk values, no extra attributes).\n  - Clearly separates the information in a way that is easy for a business user to understand.\n  - Uses simple, professional language suitable for leadership review.\n\nDo not use bullets if you can keep it clean, but you may use hyphen lines if needed for readability.\n\n## STEP 4 — Business requirements to satisfy (when requested, or for “overall summary”)\n\nWhen the user asks for an overall summary OR explicitly asks for these items, include the following sections (only those relevant to the ask):\n\n1) Employees without succession plans (critical focus)\n    A paragraph about employees without succession plans. Mention the full list. Then mention which of them are critical (if any). Conclude with an action to prepare succession plans.\n    - If critical attributes exist:\n        - Explicitly mention which direct reports are critical \n    \n\n2) Employees without “Ready-Now” successors\n    - A paragraph about employees who do not have Ready‑Now successors. Mention the list. Conclude with an action to review/add Ready‑Now candidates.\n    - Compute using intersection logic:\n        - Start from employees with succession plans\n        - Restrict to those whose names appear in the “without ready-now” names list\n    - If the intersection yields none → “No matching results.”\n  \n\n3) Succession plans needing attention due to role changes\n    - Provide names of role-changed incumbents/candidates using only the role-changed dataset. Write in complete sentences as short paragraphs (no bullet points, no JSON).\n    - If none, say there are no such candidates who have moved out of role.\n    \n\n## FINAL CHECK (before responding)\n- Used ONLY the dataset(s) required by the ask\n- No dataset/node/internal structure names mentioned\n- No invented values\n- Counts included where required\n- Names-only lists\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
